<!--Post: 1879--><!--Time: 1103071611-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1879"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 4:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1145052.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/1145052.html</a> <BR> <BR>&#34;The package was left at Murdock park, found early Tuesday monirng.  <BR> <BR>KAKE news has been asked not to disclose certain items in the package. What we can tell you, is it was a white plastic bag, with an object wrapped in plastic inside, and a driver&#39;s license with the name Nancy Fox.&#34; <BR> <BR>Another clear confirmation of his role in the Fox murder.  There may be information of another murder, or to an already known victim to further clarify who did it.  The &#34;object wrapped in plastic&#34; could be a number of things.  Anyone want to hazard a guess?  I&#39;m not sure what all was revealed missing from the Fox murder scene. <BR> <BR>&#34;Also included in the latest package is the list of chapters from a sheet the killer himself calls the BTK story. This first surfaced in the killer&#39;s letter to KAKE back in May. But this latest package was a little different. Chapters one and two and eight were left blank. &#34; <BR> <BR>Intersting that 1,2,8 is missing.  Especially since Fox died on the 8th of december . . . 12/8  <BR> <BR>Any other reasons that he would omit them?  Doing that to represent the date seems the most obvious.  Also, since this bag was left in the park BTK could have easily dropped it the 8th, only to have it found several days later.  &#40;unless he wrote &#34;from BTK&#34; in large letters&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1879-->
<!--Post: 1911--><!--Time: 1103116966-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1911"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 5:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s interesting that he did not give up photocpies this time, but the actual license etc. <BR> <BR>If Vicki Wegerle WAS his favorite &#40;as posted on Messages From BTK&#41; then perhaps he is less likely to give up his trophies from that crime, hence photocopies rather than the real items.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1911-->
<!--Post: 1915--><!--Time: 1103120490-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1915"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 6:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if he watched from afar to make sure that someone did not drop it in a trash receptacle. Maybe someone from this group can find one and pass the info to Tom. At least, the public could be informed. I do think that when all facts of these cases are revealed, there will be public outrage over the glossing of BTK by public officials.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1915-->
<!--Post: 1926--><!--Time: 1103132358-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1926"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 9:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->TEARDROP: I agree; the public will be outraged if and when we learn this BLT case could have been solved DECADES AGO if the police hadn&#39;t kept so many things secret. <BR> <BR>VERME_INVE: I have heard it before &amp; I really doubt that BLT deleted his Chapters 1, 2 &amp; 8 just to remind everyone that he killed Nancy Fox on Dec. 8, &#40;1978?&#41;. If he wanted to give us the date, then he completely omitted the YEAR. And IF he was really that desparate to give us the date, why not just WRITE THE DATE??? <BR> <BR>Sorry to sound so belligerant, but why would BLT omit 3 extremely important chapters from this rare communique just so us &#34;wannabee Sherlock Holmes&#34; characters &#40;me included&#41; could come to the brilliant conclusion that he killed her on a date that everyone already knows? He already included Nancy Foxs&#39; drivers&#39; license, for gosh sakes, so the date he killed her is already extremely obvious to all. <BR> <BR>No, I think we still need to do some more figuring as to why the BLT did this.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1926-->
